WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.710
More Thanos backstory, a Captain Marvel scene,
and multiple epic trailer shots are just some

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.640
of the things that got the chop from the final
version of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.930
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and it's time to talk deleted scenes and rejected

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:18.460
concepts that never made it into the magnificently
ambitious third Avengers movie.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.260
I've got an Infinity War giveaway running
for all my subscribers, so hit the bell and

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.840
I'll have more details later.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.029
And, obviously, spoilers ahead for the movie,
so take care if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.940
In Avengers: Infinity War, the grand villain
Thanos takes centre stage in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.120
Universe, and boy does he make an impression!

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.899
Prior to this, we'd had just brief scenes
of the Mad Titan in both Avengers post-credits

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:44.809
and short scenes with him in Guardians of
the Galaxy, so it's a bit of a shame some

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:48.120
moments with the big purple guy that were
teased in the trailers didn't make it into

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.609
the final film.

00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:53.690
For instance, although Ebony Maw told the
Black Order to 'let [Thanos] have his fun'

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:58.539
smashing the Hulk on the Asgardian ship, this
next epic line from Thanos didn't make it

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:03.350
into the movie:
"Fun isn't something one considers when balancing

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.160
the universe.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:13.540
But this does put a smile on my face."

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.400
And this shot of Thanos coming in with an
almighty punch during the Titan fight scenes

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.630
was also cut.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:22.570
Plus, there was a more extensive backstory
for the very big bad which we didn't get to

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:27.770
see because, after considering it, the Russos
felt it 'wasn't necessary for the movie.'

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.170
Some fans might have liked a touch more background
about Thanos's earlier life or younger years

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.170
on Titan.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:37.200
Thanos did mention in the movie that he was
labelled 'a mad man' for his suggestion about

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.110
fixing the planet's resources problem.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.700
But we didn't get to learn about, for example,
how he was also ostracised for being 'like

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.550
the Quasimodo of his time', as Josh Brolin
called him, which might have made the audience

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.040
feel for him more.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.510
Obviously, more backstory for the villain
would have meant a longer runtime though.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:56.900
And Marvel does also have a non-canon book
"Thanos: Titan Consumed" which will reveal

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.950
more of his origins before the events of Infinity
War.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.560
The impressive shot of Thor standing tall
after the creation of Stormbreaker with lightning

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.100
crackling around him, while Groot and Rocket
look on, was also chopped from the final film.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.750
And this shot in Nidavellir of the Asgardian
god wearing his red cape didn't make it in

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:15.750
either.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.830
I suspect both of these moments came just
before Thor used Stormbreaker's Bifrost powers

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.260
for his grand entrance in Wakanda.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.090
Although both those lightning and cape shots
are really cool, I can understand why they

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:31.280
were cut as Thor's arrival in Wakanda becomes
even more breath-taking when we go from having

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.630
seen him just about to be revived with his
new weapon and then next time we see him he's

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.550
slamming down Stormbreaker taking out the
Outriders that are overwhelming our heroes.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:44.319
"Ready"
And that line of Thor preparing himself to

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:48.050
restart the forges on Nidavellir also hit
the cutting room floor.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:52.330
And there are many scenes that were chopped
out of the Wakanda parts of the film as well.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.750
First of all, there was this scene of Bruce
Banner standing next to the Hulkbuster arm,

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.730
talking to what looks like Black Widow there.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.260
I wonder if this might have been a little
private moment between them which addressed

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.420
the pair's previous relationship.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.510
Banner and Romanoff were separated after the
Hulk ended up on the Quinjet at the end of

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.990
Age of Ultron and she doesn't see him again
until Team Cap visits the New Avengers facility

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.950
where they have an awkward little reunion
in this film.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:20.040
Then there was a shot cut of Black Widow,
Bruce Banner and War Machine watching the

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.800
alien invaders descend on Wakanda.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:26.800
And this moment with Cap trying out his new
shield in T'Challa's palace was cut from the

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.370
final movie.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.730
"Let's go."

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.459
Another Captain America and Black Panther
deleted moment was this shot of the pair on

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:38.340
the Wakandan craft as they zoom out to face
the Outriders.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.350
We never saw this very cool shot of Hulkbuster
jumping and landing.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:45.740
Instead, there was a different shot in the
movie where he jumps into the battlefield

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:50.300
which is filled with Outriders, plus of course
there was also that amusing moment when Hulkbuster

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.630
runs and falls flat on his face.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:56.709
And perhaps something many of us were hoping
to see was that epic shot of Cap leading the

00:03:56.709 --> 00:04:01.630
charge with all the heroes around him, plus
the Wakandan army and a Hulked-out Banner.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:06.530
Other than on the Asgardian ship we never
saw the Hulk do battle because Banner failing

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:11.099
to coax out the jade giant was an interesting
running theme in the movie, so this scene

00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:14.570
here was presumably edited or shot solely
for marketing purposes.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:19.919
If you wanted to see the Hulk burst out of
Hulkbuster, like this toy, you were out of

00:04:19.919 --> 00:04:20.919
luck!

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:24.990
Now, we do see a nice reunion between Steve
and Bucky in Wakanda, but it looks like there

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.289
were other Bucky scenes we didn't get to see.

00:04:27.289 --> 00:04:32.879
According to Infinity War press set visits,
after Steve and Bucky hug, Bucky says, "So,

00:04:32.879 --> 00:04:38.009
little green men, huh?" to which Black Widow
replies, "Not little, not green."

00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:42.029
And then there was a bit of Falcon and Bucky
interplay cut from the movie which would have

00:04:42.029 --> 00:04:46.449
shown Sam Wilson jokily asking Bucky, "Are
you gonna snap and kill someone if they say

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:51.050
bologna sandwich?", which is a comical call-back
to the activation codes used to trigger The

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:54.169
Winter Soldier, something we last saw in Civil
War.

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:59.199
Also during set visits, the Russo Brothers
were asked who had the best costume in Infinity

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:05.430
War and they replied Captain Marvel, adding
"Captain Marvel on set, is that official?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.860
If it's not, it's official now."

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.839
As I mentioned in my full breakdown of the
movie's post-credits scene, we did, of course,

00:05:11.839 --> 00:05:16.539
get a tease for Captain Marvel via Nick Fury's
pager, but it sounds like originally she was

00:05:16.539 --> 00:05:21.759
going to be part of the film in some way,
maybe making an actual appearance in the post-credits

00:05:21.759 --> 00:05:27.270
scene, which perhaps might have ended on a
shot of Brie Larson receiving Fury's message.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:31.061
If you go back and rewatch the trailers for
Infinity War, it's clear that a lot of the

00:05:31.061 --> 00:05:35.419
shots in the movie were changed in the marketing
material to avoid revealing spoilers.

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:40.289
We know that Thanos had five infinity stones
when he finally arrived in Wakanda, but when

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:43.840
Cap went up against him only two were shown
in the trailer.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.360
Other modified shots include this awesome
shot of Spidey swinging through Titan, which

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.509
in the final movie turned out to be a shot
of Spidey with his Iron Spider legs plus he

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:55.040
was also carrying Mantis!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.379
In this New York scene, in the movie, Tony's
new nano-tech Iron Man suit was already wrapping

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:04.319
itself around him, but in the trailer we just
see Tony with his normal clothes.

00:06:04.319 --> 00:06:09.059
And in the first trailer, we saw an unarmed
Cap fighting Outriders, whereas in the final

00:06:09.059 --> 00:06:11.949
movie he had his new shields in these shots.

00:06:11.949 --> 00:06:15.830
These edits to the marketing material are
similar to how Thor's missing eye was handled

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.309
in the trailers for Thor: Ragnarok.

00:06:18.309 --> 00:06:21.780
Interestingly, another way the Russo's tried
to stop the plot leaking out was that they

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.710
actually gave fake scripts to a lot of the
actors.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.990
And it's possible that some of them didn't
even know they were going to fade away at

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:31.060
the end of the film when they were shooting
those scenes.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.389
Other deleted scenes and alternate takes which
the Russos have said may show up on the Blu-ray

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:38.659
came about because of the large amount of
improv on set.

00:06:38.659 --> 00:06:43.249
The directors were bringing together characters
from movies with very distinct tones, and

00:06:43.249 --> 00:06:47.439
often those characters were meeting each other
for the first time, and so the filmmakers

00:06:47.439 --> 00:06:51.560
spent extra time making sure they got the
chemistry right in those scenes, allowing

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.689
the actors to improvise for several takes
after doing an initial couple of takes from

00:06:55.689 --> 00:06:56.689
the script.

00:06:56.689 --> 00:07:01.479
For example, Thor's never heard of or met
the Guardians when he lands on their ship.

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:02.479
"Eww.

00:07:02.479 --> 00:07:03.479
Wipers, wipers!"

00:07:03.479 --> 00:07:04.860
"Get it off!"

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:07.139
"How is this dude still alive?"

00:07:07.139 --> 00:07:08.889
"He is not a dude.

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:10.629
You're a dude."

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:12.800
"This is a man."

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:16.819
"A handsome, muscular man."

00:07:16.819 --> 00:07:24.219
"It's like his muscles are made of Katardi
metal fibers."

00:07:24.219 --> 00:07:29.619
And, given the humour we saw play out in that
scene, I can imagine there's some funny alternate

00:07:29.619 --> 00:07:31.039
or extended takes.

00:07:31.039 --> 00:07:34.870
It was initially reported that the running
time for Avengers: Infinity War was going

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:39.699
to be 156 minutes, but then a few weeks later
it was officially announced that the final

00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:45.469
runtime was 149 minutes, seven minutes less,
bringing in the movie to just under two and

00:07:45.469 --> 00:07:46.860
a half hours.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.689
It seems like this could be a possible explanation
for where some of these missing scenes went

00:07:50.689 --> 00:07:55.369
as the filmmakers may have been editing out
bits they felt brought the movie's pace down.

00:07:55.369 --> 00:07:59.379
Another thing that never made it into the
movie from the early drafts was an idea the

00:07:59.379 --> 00:08:01.599
screenwriters came up with for a giant snake!

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:06.089
In an interview with Entertainment Tonight,
co-writer Christopher Markus said, "We were

00:08:06.089 --> 00:08:08.830
sort of running on empty and we were like,
"Snake?

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:09.830
Big snake?

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:11.419
Let's try big snake."

00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:13.860
And then everyone went insane."

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:18.089
I imagine the writers might have been thinking
of a character like the Asgardian Midgard

00:08:18.089 --> 00:08:21.929
Serpent from the comics, which was hinted
at briefly in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:08:21.929 --> 00:08:26.970
"There was one time when we were children,
he transformed himself into a snake, and he

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:27.970
knows that I love snakes."

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:31.589
"So, I went to pick up the snake to admire
it, and he transformed back into himself and

00:08:31.589 --> 00:08:32.960
he was like, 'Yeah, it's me!'

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:33.960
And he stabbed me.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.199
"We were eight at the time."

00:08:36.199 --> 00:08:40.409
The enormous snake didn't make it into the
final draft though and it's probably for the

00:08:40.409 --> 00:08:45.519
best given how packed Infinity War was already;
also, depending on how its scenes played out

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:49.910
and the creature's design, it might have felt
too visually similar to the Leviathans from

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.000
the first Avengers.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.480
Now, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
had been included in the movie?

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.029
And what do you think about fake scenes being
shot?

00:08:58.029 --> 00:09:02.600
Let me know in the comments and make sure
you're subscribed for a chance to win a very

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.940
cool Infinity War Funko Pop!

